The experiments verified the effectiveness and efficiency of our proposal, demonstrating that while the adaptation of the regret-ratio based algorithm hd-rrms fails to provide a rank-regret representative as its outputs had large rank-regrets. In contrast, 2drrr, mdrrr, andmdrc found small sets with small rank-regrets. Although the rank-regret of their outputs can be larger than k in our experiments and measurements those were always below k.madrr provided small outputs that as expected, always guarantees the rank-regret of k. The quadratic 2drrr and the hitting-set based algorithm mdrrr scaled up to a limit, whereas mdrc had low running time at all scales.

